- [memory-api/crates/session-api/src/tool_metrics.rs](memory-api/crates/session-api/src/tool_metrics.rs#L1587-L1679) — added late-copy upgrade/idempotency tests.

## Dedup logic before/after

Before (first-wins drop):

```rust
let mut counted_tool_call_ids = BTreeSet::<String>::new();
...
if let Some(tool_call_id) = event.tool_call_id.clone() {
    if !counted_tool_call_ids.insert(tool_call_id) {
        return;
    }
}
```

After (rank-aware upgrade):

```rust
let mut tracked_calls = BTreeMap::<String, TrackedToolCall>::new();
...
if let Some(tool_call_id) = event.tool_call_id.clone() {
    if let Some(tracked) = tracked_calls.get_mut(&tool_call_id) {
        if let (Some(output_chars), Some(output_source)) = (output_chars, output_source) {
            if new_rank > tracked.output_rank {
                // overwrite in place, never recount
            }
        }
        return;
    }
}
```

Rank order: `hook_payload` (3) > `spill_file` (2) > `transcript_turn` (1) > unspecified (0). Ties and lower ranks are no-ops, so replays stay idempotent.

## What the sync path now does

`capture_copilot_transcript_with_tool_response` parses once and persists immediately — no `std::thread::sleep`, no retry. The late override reconciles on the next hook invocation (e.g. `Stop`), because:

1. `merge_events` keys events by `captured_event_key`, which fingerprints `data_json`; the override-free and override-rich copies have different keys and are both kept.
2. `record_event_tool_call` then upgrades the already-counted `tool_call_id` when the later copy has a higher-fidelity `output_source`.

